authoring step, not a consent vote[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The finalizer declaration asks an agent only to author commit [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]messages. Leaving a tree dirty becomes a rare, typed, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]host-adjudicated deferral that is corrected while the agent is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]still alive and never destroys a run.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]finalizer_commit_authoring.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/finalizer_commit_authoring.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-sp[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-sp/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Typed deferral and a non-failing refusal policy in Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: add the typed deferral-reason enum, the `defer` refusal policy, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the non-failing Deferred statuses to the Rust finalizer wire, then [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release the crate.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the released core floor and the deferral config schema[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adopt: raise the sase_core_rs floor, mirror the new wire records in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase.core.finalizer_wire, and accept `refusal: fail | defer` in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]finalizer config.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adjudicate deferrals at submit time instead of after the turn[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]adjudicate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adjudicate: replace the free-text `refuse` action with typed `defer` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decisions and make `sase final submit` reject unfounded deferrals as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repairable validation errors while the agent still holds its context.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A deliberate deferral escape hatch that does not fail the run[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]escape[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adjudicate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]escape: add `sase final defer`, honor `refusal: defer` in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]controller, and report a deferred turn as a completed run with a dirty [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tree that the user is told about, instead of a FAILED run with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stranded workspace.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Publish the commit consent model where agents actually read it[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]consent[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adjudicate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]consent: carry the commit-by-default rule and per-repository provenance [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]evidence in `sase final context` output, rewrite the `/sase_final` skill[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]around authoring, and remove the self-contradiction in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declaration-recovery prompt.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Historical regression corpus, live acceptance, telemetry, and [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]docs[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after escape, consent[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: replay every historical refusal as a regression fixture, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prove the protocol live end to end, add refusal and deferral telemetry, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and synchronize the finalizer documentation.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-sp","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-sp.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-34c9c4137d9505036b795e85eaa00c62","started_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:53.258327+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"19c4609a8b68f8ac80c04e0232932b0087969a674f201dfbe07406e0e97b6809","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-sp.2--mon-0/chat.md","size_bytes":6343},"commits":{"digest":"a43bb5c313d075e39b6fbf2f0f3983572403a1df0469d40a0d348b3b0db8de75","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-sp.2--mon-0/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"c0b3ccb361da2464c6982c57432b418363aa006dc8b420746184479a6c367eb9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-sp.2--mon-0/meta.json","size_bytes":641},"state":{"digest":"6e9c0b4842cb8fd5a8b42867e5a4aa7035eb1c8f1f557eb855e807ee645aa850","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-sp.2--mon-0/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-sp.2--mon-0","local_name":"sase-sp.2--mon-0","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-sp","agent_clan_generation":"20260824092013","agent_family":"sase-sp.2","agent_family_role":"mon-0","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","reasoning_effort":"high","role_suffix":"mon-0","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-sp.2"},"source_run_id":"run-4eba1de0ced291c3216619a852925a9e","started_at":"2026-08-24T14:47:46.882183+00:00","state":"failed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_